WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- First, I want
(audience claps)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.180
to talk about a beauty influencer

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.040
with a special talent for storytelling.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.160
Literally, I've heard so many
people tell me about her.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.330
She's a makeup artist turned
true crime phenomenon.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.040
Each week, Bailey showcases
the latest in makeup

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.790
while dishing the juiciest details

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.360
of notorious crime cases,
which is so hilarious.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.250
And I would have never put those together.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.420
Her viral YouTube series,
"Murder, Mystery, and Makeup"

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.240
has more than 400 million views.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.730
Let's get her on the line right now.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.280
What's up Bailey?

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.790
Hi Kelly.
(audience claps and cheers)

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.030
- Hi.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.903
I mean, how did you come up with it?

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:35.223
- I don't know.

00:00:35.223 --> 00:00:36.240
I mean, like, I've always been fascinated

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.490
with true crime and makeup.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.010
When I was a kid, my mom
was a 9-1-1 dispatcher,

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.800
and she used to take me to work with her,

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.120
and I would like listen
in to the phone calls,

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.440
which we laugh about it
now, but looking back,

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.530
it probably wasn't the best idea

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.363
for her to take me
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:00:50.363 --> 00:00:51.940
to work, you know (laughs)?

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.690
And then like, so I've just been obsessed

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.680
with true crime for as
long as I can remember.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.240
And then as far as makeup goes,

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.640
I mean I wasn't allowed
to wear makeup growing up

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.990
until about in my '20s is
when I started to dabble,

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.030
and I got a job at Sephora,

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.580
and then I started my YouTube channel,

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:13.490
and it just, I mean, it
just, I'm here (laughs).

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:14.323
It's a lot.
(audience laughs)

00:01:14.323 --> 00:01:15.410
- No, it's taken over.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:16.530
Well, I know several people

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.070
that think you're hilarious by the way.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.680
They're like, "Oh my God, she's hilarious

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.920
while telling me a story."

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:22.570
So what surprised you the most

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.320
like researching all these stories?

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.880
- I think a lot, well, I
used to be a big believer

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.740
that some people were just born evil,

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.830
like most people were just born evil.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.840
But after doing these stories for so long,

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.250
I realized that it all comes down to like

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:40.360
how they were raised and
also their upbringing,

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:41.950
their relationship with their parents,

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:45.860
and then head trauma is like
a common thread in a lot of,

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.240
some of the worst killers.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.150
And I mean, it's just bizarre.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.760
So I think a lot of the
times we personally think

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.540
like these monsters are monsters,

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.070
and really they're not.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:01.100
They're just like the normal
people who live next door

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.240
who just had a really rough life (laughs).

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.310
Which isn't an excuse.
- Well that

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.539
is terrifying news.

00:02:07.539 --> 00:02:08.995
That is like.
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.310
- I know, I know, I don't.
- I mean, we have a whole

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:13.590
campaign on here called,
you know, good neighbor,

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:16.040
and I'm now terrified
officially of my neighbors

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.750
who might not be good, who
might've, I don't know,

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:19.583
fell off the horse
- Sorry.

00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:21.850
- and bumped their head
and might kill me now.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:22.940
That's why I can't, okay,

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:24.350
I can't get into true crime a lot,

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.030
because I was, I was so invested,

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:29.080
and I watched every "Dateline"
thing, I got so into it.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.710
And then I started become
physically terrified,

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.820
didn't sleep, 'cause I was so terrified.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.250
I was like, so they
probably know that one guy,

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.383
he got to the third floor,
so they could get up here.

00:02:36.383 --> 00:02:39.090
I mean, I sit here and
like play out scenarios.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.040
So I got so crazy, but I think
it's hilarious what you do.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.620
I think it's so innovative too.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:44.660
Nobody's else is doing it.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:46.640
So thank you Bailey for joining us.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.473
- Thank you so much

00:02:47.473 --> 00:02:48.390
for having me.
(audience cheers and claps)

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.310
- Absolutely.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.510
And you look beautiful,

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:52.317
so well done on your makeup (laughs).

